  {
    "sha": "901e2a227ce9e992503fa71bc480d20046ce1bb9",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDkwMWUyYTIyN2NlOWU5OTI1MDNmYTcxYmM0ODBkMjAwNDZjZTFiYjk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-16T04:27:11Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-16T04:27:11Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(cl): keep world position out of the break connection allowance\n\nThe allowance that joins a framed cap to the model surface scaled with\nthe surface's absolute Z. Translated to z = 1e14, a cap a representable\n0.09375 mm under the surface was joined and a real gouge above it was\ncleared.\n\nA span now joins only across a fixed 1e-9 mm. Roundoff is bounded per\nplane crossing from the column's offset to the segment, which a\ntranslation does not change, and a span is used at its certain part\nonly: latest possible start, earliest possible end. Each end plane is\nmeasured from its own endpoint.\n\nPinned by a_far_z_translation_cannot_connect_a_detached_cap (sim, through\ncredit_breaks), connection_allowance_does_not_grow_with_world_position,\nan_uncertain_interval_end_is_never_read_in_favour_of_the_cut and\na_column_at_a_vertex_of_barely_sloped_segments_keeps_its_credit (cl).\n\nRefs #1891\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
      "tree": {
